{'symbol': 'FDX', 'date': '2021-03-01 10:14:00', 'title': 'FEDEX PREPARES FOR COVID-19 VACCINE VOLUME GROWTH, BEGINS SHIPPING NEWLY APPROVED VACCINE', 'text': "MEMPHIS, TENN.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--FEDEX EXPRESS, A SUBSIDIARY OF FEDEX CORP. (NYSE: FDX) AND THE WORLD'S LARGEST EXPRESS TRANSPORTATION COMPANY, ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT IT HAS BEGUN SHIPPING THE NEWLY APPROVED COVID-19 VACCINE ON BEHALF OF MCKESSON CORP. TO DOSING CENTERS THROUGHOUT THE UNITED STATES. THE COMPANY HAS SHIPPED MILLIONS OF COVID-19 VACCINES SINCE U.S. DISTRIBUTION BEGAN IN MID-DECEMBER 2020 AND IS PREPARED TO SCALE UP TO ACCOMMODATE ANTICIPATED GROWTH IN VACCINE VOLUME THROUGHOUT THE"}